</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.5. </span>Online Experiments</h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We validated the real-world performance and scalability of HiSAC through a large-scale online deployment in the “Guess What You Like” homepage feed of the Taobao recommendation system, followed by a controlled two-week A/B test involving hundreds of millions of daily active users.
As shown in Table <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 4.4. Hyperparameters Analysis ‣ 4. Experiments ‣ HiSAC: Hierarchical Sparse Activation Compression for Ultra-long Sequence Modeling in Recommenders" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, the proposed approach consistently improves all monitored business metrics.
Specifically, the click-through rate (CTR) increases by <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.65\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.65</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.65\%</annotation></semantics></math> and the item page view (IPV) by <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.93\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.93</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.93\%</annotation></semantics></math>, demonstrating that enhanced preference modeling leads to more engaging recommendations in a live production environment.
Moreover, the conversion-through-click rate (CTCVR) is lifted by <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.24\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.24</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.24\%</annotation></semantics></math>, and the number of orders increases by <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.56\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.56</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.56\%</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating that the additional user engagements translate into high-quality clicks and more purchases, thereby generating substantial business value.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We proposed HiSAC, a hierarchical semantic-agent compression framework for modeling multi-granular user interests in large-scale recommendation.
Combining Residual RQ-VAE encoding, hierarchical voting, and soft-routing, HiSAC captures diverse interests while mitigating quantization errors from hard assignment.
The framework has been deployed on a large-scale e-commerce platform, where it achieved a 1.65% improvement in online CTR over strong baselines, demonstrating its practical value and effectiveness.</p>
</div>
</section>
